          /^\s*(tracked files read|population[^:]*|baseline entries[^:]*):\s*(\d+)/
          mode PER_LINE; renamed → match. It is an ALTERNATION: the label it still matches is another alternative, so the host sees a match and loses only the figure it wanted. That is a QUIETER failure than a null, not a safer one.
  LIVE survivors that survive via an alternation        : 1
  post-hoc 2's figure for this cell was 6 of 7, and host mode also reads 6 of 7.
  The FIGURE is unmoved and the REASON is different: post-hoc 2 reached 6 with
  probe-baseline.mjs:30 scored on a dead whole-text cell; host mode reaches 6 with the
  same site scored LIVE-and-surviving. Same number, two causes — which is why the
  corrected drive was worth running even though it did not move the count.
  APPEND: 1 of 13 patterns break, and it is the END-ANCHORED site his §2 names —
  so his regex reasoning is CONFIRMED at the pattern level. Of those breaks,
  0 belong to an instrument that reads live gate output.
